      "content": "thanks. i want to look closer at the \"urban cool\" and \"niche\" categories. for example, i'm seeing a lot of trends coming out of AAVE (African American Vernacular English) and certain Latino-influenced slang, like people using terms like \"no cap,\" \"finna,\" or specific drill music aesthetics. \n\nhow would you characterize the \"sophistication\" level of these specific linguistic styles compared to something like \"preppy\" or \"corporate\" branding language? i'm trying to figure out if they're viewed as \"refined\" for luxury brands or if they're strictly relegated to \"street\" or more \"low-brow\" demographic targeting.",
